 or hard-to-test interfaces\n5. Pass-through layers that fail the deletion test\n6. Per-loop or per-provider branches that should be adapter-dispatched (CONTEXT.md emphasizes auto-discovery)\n7. Status TSV / record schemas that drift between writers and readers\n8. Things that look like the same concern split across multiple files\n9. Long files (>500 lines) that may be hiding multiple deep modules\n\nFocus on **substantial** architectural improvements, not nitpicks. Skip cosmetic or trivial issues. The previous convergence runs (see docs/plans/converge/ logs) have reportedly exhausted obvious improvements — be discerning.\n\nRead the lib/*.sh files including loop-launcher.sh, run.sh, worker.sh, agent.sh, harden-core.sh, converge-core.sh, loops.sh, providers/*.sh, loops/*.sh. Skim the cmd/ scripts. Note line counts for the larger files.\n\nReport under 600 words with a ranked list (highest leverage first) of candidate improvements. Use specific file:line citations."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1521,"cache_read_input_tokens":41667,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1521},"output_tokens":53,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8f5db91c-a278-450c-98f6-32d4d1454f5d","uuid":"30ccff48-f610-44ec-8760-a15490e4e8cc","request_id":"req_011CbSidFLaGu4fJaeCeqCED"}
