{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01XZWRqVKdtMp58zfFMwKuXm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Prior convergence runs say codebase converged. Caveat: per memory, `bash tests/*` not in allowlist → cannot validate refactors headlessly. Skill's own protocol says present candidates → ask which → grill → then implement. \"Do all\" violates that flow + risks breaking 6366 lines of bash without test coverage.\n\nExplore agent found 7 candidates. Honest assessment:\n\n**1. Converge overseer parser fragility** (`lib/converge-core.sh:231-385`) — already addressed by recent `bfffbd5` (lenient parser + raw-response logging). Nothing left worth doing here without seeing real-world failures from the new shape.\n\n**2. `harden-core.sh` (1977 lines) hides 3 concerns** — rubric lifecycle, reviewer/ledger orchestration, ratification engine. Split candidate. Big refactor (~500-700 lines move). High value for AI-navigability. Risky without tests.\n\n**3. TSV schema fragility across `run.sh` + `worker.sh` + `harden-core.sh` + `converge-core.sh`** — harden's findings ledger uses positional printf (lines 521-574), converge overseer returns via globals (`ALMANAC_CONVERGE_VERDICT` etc.). Should use `almanac_loop_tsv_record_set`. Medium refactor, ~6 callsites in harden, 4 in converge.\n\n**4. Conductor provider not memoized** — premature optimization, not real friction. Skip.\n\n**5. Prompt generation entangled with orchestration in `converge-core.sh:63-142`** — pure template fns called from impure orchestration. Moderate cleanup. Section delimiters duplicated in writer + parser. Splittable into `lib/converge-prompts.sh`.\n\n**6. `feedback.sh` shallow marker table** — 40% of module is config-as-code. Data-driven table won't change anything important. Skip.\n\n**7. Unify converge + harden into a convergence-loop framework** — biggest leverage, biggest risk. Both run outer-round → workers → adjudicate → continue/steer/stop. Would extract a 4th seam. Massive blast radius. Definitely needs tests.\n\nRecommendation: don't do all. Most leverage = #2 (harden split) and #3 (TSV unification). Both need test validation. Prior 7-round convergence already declared no major improvements remain.\n\nWhat do you want?\n- A) apply #3 only (smallest blast radius, can spot-check)  \n- B) apply #2 + #3 + open PR, you run tests\n- C) apply nothing, accept prior convergence verdict\n- D) something else"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":978,"cache_read_input_tokens":50893,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":978},"output_tokens":44,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8f5db91c-a278-450c-98f6-32d4d1454f5d","uuid":"56647bad-ddb1-4d4b-8f49-57718b833227","request_id":"req_011CbSimZNkb3CtLD9PMZxGr"}
